00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.630
I was like talking about like
having two knee surgeries

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.977
and people were like
talking about real shit.

00:04:21.977 --> 00:04:26.150
Just for context for like what
are some of the challenges

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.554
that people overcame in this book?

00:04:28.554 --> 00:04:29.850
- I mean we have many stories.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.950
One we share our personal stories

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.930
and challenges that we faced.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.470
We have a person in the book

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.560
who was burned over 90% of his body.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:41.020
He was given greater
than 100% mortality rate

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.437
at age, he was a teenager,
and his mother asked him,

00:04:43.437 --> 00:04:45.327
"Do you wanna live or do you wanna die?

00:04:45.327 --> 00:04:47.390
"And if you wanna live you have to fight."

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.350
and so he chose to fight, obviously

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.093
and he survived and he overcame.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.850
Given a mortality rate of
100% that's almost miraculous

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.785
that he was able to kind
of overcome the situation.

00:04:57.785 --> 00:05:00.257
- From a medical standpoint,
I have a question

00:05:00.257 --> 00:05:03.193
I have a feeling this is gonna
be a tough thing to answer.

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:05.810
