everybody who's listening.

00:46:33.380 --> 00:46:34.213
Why were you having a conversation?

00:46:34.213 --> 00:46:36.020
Are you business associates or friends?

00:46:36.020 --> 00:46:39.210
- Yeah, we both have our own
foundations, run foundations.

00:46:39.210 --> 00:46:41.920
And his foundation honored
me for the work that I do.

00:46:41.920 --> 00:46:42.753
- [Gary] And that's how
you got to know each other?

00:46:42.753 --> 00:46:46.360
- So I met him and I hired him

00:46:46.360 --> 00:46:48.490
and his friends to
speak to all of our kids

00:46:48.490 --> 00:46:51.150
in our organization because
their story was so impactful.

00:46:51.150 --> 00:46:51.983
- [Gary] Yep, got it.

00:46:51.983 --> 00:46:53.070
- And we were on a flight home

00:46:53.070 --> 00:46:55.300
from one of our baseball clinics in Tampa

00:46:55.300 --> 00:46:57.640
and he started talking
about this book idea.

00:46:57.640 --> 00:46:59.060
He had a book idea,

00:46:59.060 --> 00:47:01.870
but it was more along the
medical side of things

00:47:01.870 --> 00:47:03.210
and I was like, come on Sam,

00:47:03.210 --> 00:47:05.020
don't make me read another medical book.

00:47:05.020 --> 00:47:06.300
I'll read it to support you

00:47:06.300 --> 00:47:07.470
but look, why don't you do something

00:47:07.470 --> 00:47:09.240
that everyone can relate to?

00:47:09.240 --> 00:47:12.090
And, I don't even remember how
it exactly it was brought up,

00:47:12.090 --> 00:47:14.750
but he brought up something
about me going through treatment

00:47:14.750 --> 00:47:16.730
and how I was one of these people

00:47:16.730 --> 00:47:18.630
who had overcome adversity.

00:47:18.630 --> 00:47:20.610
And I said, no, no-no-no,

00:47:20.610 --> 00:47:22.980
like I just didn't wanna leave college

00:47:22.980 --> 00:47:24.750
and leave my friends and move back home.

00:47:24.750 --> 00:47:26.542
Like really, I truly believed that.

00:47:26.542 --> 00:47:27.390
- I believe that, yeah.

00:47:27.390 --> 00:47:30.050
- I did not want to stop life

00:47:30.050 --> 00:47:31.400
and he's like but the fact

00:47:31.400 --> 00:47:35.200
that you look at it
that way is so strange.

00:47:35.200 --> 00:47:38.780
You know it's not normal that
you just say, oh, cancer,

00:47:38.780 --> 00:47:42.110
okay well I'm just gonna
stay in school and finish up

00:47:42.110 --> 00:47:43.980
and take a flight back and forth,

00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:45.620
which luckily I was fortunate enough,

00:47:45.620 --> 00:47:48.070
my family could support me to do that.

00:47:48.070 --> 00:47:52.470
But you know it was eye
opening for me to know

00:47:52.470 --> 00:47:56.230
that I actually had something
inside of me that would,

00:47:56.230 --> 00:47:57.981
that had prepared me to go through that.

00:47:57.981 --> 00:48:00.275
And that was why I was on this search

00:48:00.275 --> 00:48:02.580
through doing this project to find out

00:48:02.580 --> 00:48:04.750
what were those things
that I had inside of me

00:48:04.750 --> 00:48:06.300
so that I could use them moving forward,

00:48:06.300 --> 00:48:08.403
so that I could teach my son about them

00:48:08.403 --> 00:48:10.310
and teach others about it.

00:48:10.310 --> 00:48:12.810
Because that was important to
me with our foundation work,

00:48:12.810 --> 00:48:15.867
with teaching kids how they do
have these things within them

00:48:15.867 --> 00:48:17.500
and a lot of times we suppress them,

00:48:17.500 --> 00:48:21.190
we don't even know they exist within us.

00:48:21.190 --> 00:48:22.090
- I love it.

00:48:22.090 --> 00:48:23.296
Eytan, thanks for such
a great question, bro.

00:48:23.296 --> 00:48:24.900
- [Eytan] All right, guys, take care.

00:48:24.900 --> 00:48:26.140
- [Sampson] Take care.

